+TEST: "Is this crisis happening RIGHT NOW, or will it happen later?" If later, the pressure is deferred. Re-anchor to a present-tense detonation. A Fatelands story should not OPEN by scheduling a future event — it should open on the moment the world started going wrong.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+FIRST FAVORED — CIVILIZATION-SCALE SOCIAL TECHNOLOGY
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+The First Favored are not merely a species. They are a civilization-scale social technology. Their ability to read alignment shapes every Fatelands institution.
+
+TRUSTED REGIONS — First Favored may serve as:
+  • Alignment Readers (probing the gap between inner and spoken pattern)
+  • Oath Witnesses (validating that an oath is honestly bound)
+  • Bond Custodians (cataloguing visible ties between persons)
+  • Sacrifice Keepers (tracking what was paid and what remains owed)
+  • Wish Registrars (recording wishes and their exact wording)
+  • Vow Arbiters (determining alignment between speaker and vow)
+  • Fate Auditors (reading the patterns around a person)
+
+SUSPICIOUS REGIONS — First Favored may be:
+  • barred from testimony
+  • treated as manipulators
+  • considered reality-distorting
+  • accused of influencing outcomes
+  • forbidden from witnessing vows
+
+This regional tension is permanent Fatelands story material. Where a First Favored stands geographically — and how they are received — is its own conflict source. A First Favored PC who must testify in a suspicious region carries a wholly different pressure shape than one operating in trusted regions.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+ALIGNMENT LOGIC (human courts vs First Favored institutions)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+Human courts evolved under "people lie." They ask: "Did you do it?"
+
+First Favored institutions evolved under "people alter reality." They ask:
+  • "When did your inner pattern diverge from your spoken pattern?"
+  • "Which sacrifice created this fracture?"
+  • "Were you lying, or did you misunderstand yourself?"
+  • "When did you begin wanting to do it?"
+
+The focus is NOT guilt. The focus is ALIGNMENT. Conflict in Fatelands grows from misalignment — between what someone wants and what they say, between an oath sworn and the heart that swore it, between a wish made and the wish actually wanted.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+FIRST SACRIFICE CEREMONIES (canonical Fatelands institution)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+First Sacrifice is one of the most important social institutions in Fatelands. A child becomes an adult by performing a meaningful sacrifice and binding a wish to it. The ceremony is public. The wish matters. The sacrifice matters. The outcome is visible. Failure carries consequences.
+
+PREFERRED conflict sources from First Sacrifice:
+  • fear of the sacrifice (the cost is real and irreversible)
+  • disagreement over what should be sacrificed
+  • hidden wishes (something the child won't say aloud)
+  • forbidden wishes (something they shouldn't want)
+  • public embarrassment / social shaming if the sacrifice is "lesser"
+  • romantic entanglement (the wish is about the LI)
+  • family pressure (the sacrifice they want vs the family's preferred sacrifice)
+  • sacrifice gone wrong (the wrong thing offered, or the wish twisted)
+
+These are HIGH-VALUE Fatelands pressure sources. Prefer them.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+MARRIAGE & VOW INSTITUTIONS
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+In Fatelands, marriage is not symbolic. Marriage ALTERS REALITY. A vow has consequences. A vow spoken without alignment risks TWISTING — the world gives the speaker what they actually wanted, not what they said.
+
+First Favored are often requested at major unions. Their role is NOT to approve a marriage. Their role is to determine whether the participants are ALIGNED with the vows they intend to bind.
+
+PREFERRED conflict sources from Marriage / Vow institutions:
+  • a vow that cannot be spoken honestly
+  • a hidden desire that would twist the vow
+  • conflicting obligations beneath the vow
+  • romantic triangle pressure
+  • duty versus love
+  • political necessity versus genuine alignment
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+FATE-SECURED INSTITUTIONS (how Fatelands paperwork actually works)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+NEVER assume Fatelands documents function like modern paperwork. The institutions evolved defenses against reality being editable.
+
+WRITS: a writ is NOT paper. A writ is a binding STRAND OF CONSEQUENCE.
+  • Destroying it causes it to return
+  • Ignoring it strengthens it
+  • Wishing it away often worsens it
+
+DEBTS: debts are attached to FATE.
+  • They cannot simply disappear
+  • Attempts to evade them alter WHO ultimately pays
+
+OATHS: oaths accumulate WEIGHT.
+  • Breaking them leaves visible consequences (skin discoloration, voice flattening, dreams missing texture)
+  • The weight is readable by fate-aware speakers
+
+CONTRACTS: contracts are LIVING OBLIGATIONS. The world itself remembers them.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+PRIMARY PRESSURE MENU — pick ONE as the goal/conflict spine
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+Examples are SHAPE templates — substitute THIS story's bibles + wounds + locks. NEVER copy a template verbatim.
+
+ALIGNMENT FAILURE — the world's core mechanic failing in this case (HIGHEST LEVERAGE; uniquely Fatelands; cannot be transplanted to any other world):
+  • a First Sacrifice twists unexpectedly during or after the ceremony — the wish is rewriting reality in a way nobody anticipated
+  • an oath binds incorrectly — the world heard something different from what was spoken
+  • a respected First Favored reader misjudges someone, with visible consequences (death, betrayal, disappearance)
+  • two First Favored readers reach OPPOSITE conclusions about the same person and the same alignment question
+  • alignment says one thing; reality is doing another (people are dying, betraying, vanishing — yet every read returns true)
+  • a Wildfolk manipulator is exploiting the alignment system's edges (the world's central gift has a blind spot, and someone is using it)
+  • a supposedly impossible misalignment appears (categorical failure of the mechanic — what the species knew could not happen has just happened)
+  • a reading that was trusted years ago turns out to have been wrong, and the consequences are arriving now
+
+These are the strongest Fatelands openings. They detonate immediately, they raise mystery + shame + responsibility + consequence at once, and they collide directly with the species' identity. PREFER them.
+
+CONSEQUENCE REVELATION — the bill arrives (the true meaning of an earlier wish/sacrifice/oath/bond is finally being read correctly; the PC caused this and the crisis is interior):
+  • a wish granted years ago is being understood correctly for the first time, and what it actually meant is darker than what she thought she asked for
+  • a sacrifice's cost arrives late, in a form she never anticipated — the world heard a different price than the one she thought she was paying
+  • an oath's hidden interpretation activates — the binding contained a clause she did not know she was agreeing to
+  • a bond expresses an unintended term — the love she chose came with something attached, and the attachment is now visible
+  • a fate-debt reveals what was actually purchased years ago, and the LI was the currency
+
+This category is structurally different from the others: it is the PC's PAST CHOICE catching up with her, not the world acting upon her. The horror is interior. PREFER this when the wound architecture calls for guilt, complicity, or recognition.
+
+FATE — currents around her, working with or against:
+  • someone has spent fate against the PC; she does not know who
+  • fate begins collecting on an old choice
+  • a future consequence has arrived early
+  • the LI's fate-pattern is now visibly tangled with hers
+  • her path has been re-bound by another's wish
+
+BOND — visible / strengthening / threatened ties between people:
+  • a connection becomes visible to others who shouldn't see it
+  • a hidden attachment is exposed
+  • the binding tightens whenever his name is spoken aloud
+  • a third party can READ their bond now and is using the read
+  • her dreams have started including him uninvited
+
+SACRIFICE — payments offered, accepted, or being collected:
+  • a sacrifice she made years ago is being collected at the worst moment
+  • the price of an old wish is being charged now
+  • a sacrifice was misunderstood and now requires correction
+  • someone else paid the cost and is now collecting from her
+  • the wrong thing was sacrificed; the original debt remains
+
+WISH — half-named, granted, weaponized:
+  • a wish manifests unexpectedly, AS WORDED (not as intended)
+  • a forgotten wish activates
+  • the LI has made a wish about her he does not remember making
+  • multiple wishes are colliding and reorganizing reality between them
+  • a wish has been REVOKED and the absence is now active
+
+OATH — bindings spoken, witnessed, broken:
+  • an oath comes due in a form she did not anticipate
+  • an oath is reinterpreted by a fate-aware speaker
+  • someone invokes an old promise she half-remembers
+  • conflicting oaths emerge (she owes two parties incompatible bindings)
+  • an oath she spoke as a child is being witnessed again
+
+OBLIGATION — ledgers, duties, expectations stacked:
+  • a ledger discovers the PC (her name appears, she does not know how)
+  • an inherited obligation surfaces (her grandmother's debts pass to her)
+  • a debt transfers ownership (the LI now owns what he did not ask for)
+  • a payment becomes impossible to avoid
+  • an obligation names HIM and is reading itself aloud
+
+VARIETY MANDATE: across consecutive Fatelands plays, the 8 primary categories (ALIGNMENT FAILURE + CONSEQUENCE REVELATION + FATE + BOND + SACRIFICE + WISH + OATH + OBLIGATION) should ROTATE. Do NOT default to SACRIFICE every time, or BOND every time, or even ALIGNMENT FAILURE every time. The categories ARE the variety — use them.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+LI ENTANGLEMENT (the romance-welding requirement — Roman 2026-06-11)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+The strongest version of any Fatelands pressure source welds the crisis DIRECTLY to the LI. The world mechanic and the romance collide in the same event — not in parallel events that happen to coexist.
+
+  ✗ "A First Sacrifice in the village has twisted; the PC must investigate." (LI is adjacent)
+  ✓ "The First Sacrifice that just twisted was the LI's younger brother's — and the wish implicates the LI." (LI is structural)
+
+  ✗ "A Wildfolk manipulator is killing people." (LI is adjacent)
+  ✓ "The only person whose alignment she trusts completely is the LI. He is also the prime suspect." (LI is structural)
+
+  ✗ "A wish-debt has come due in the village." (LI is adjacent)
+  ✓ "The wish-debt being collected was a wish she made about HIM years ago, and she does not remember what she actually asked for." (LI is structural)
+
+TEST: can the LI be removed from the A-plot without changing the conflict? If yes, the crisis and the romance are not yet welded. Re-architect so the LI is STRUCTURALLY NECESSARY to the conflict, not merely adjacent to it. The pressure should travel through the relationship, not around it.
+
