+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+THE FOUR LIGHTHOUSES — FATELANDS EMOTIONAL TERRITORY (Roman 2026-06-11)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+The four lighthouses are NOT four templates. They are the FOUR CORNERS of the emotional territory Fatelands occupies. Every Fatelands story should sit somewhere on the map between them.
+
+THE MAP:
+
+                    RELATIONSHIP ←————————————→ IDENTITY
+
+                    BROKEN VOW-BOND              THE FOLD
+                    "vow-bonds are secure"       "there is one version of me"
+
+
+                    WRONG WISH                   THE SYZYGY
+                    "I understand my desires"    "the past is fixed"
+
+                    PAST CHOICE ←————————————→ COSMOLOGY
+
+THE UNIFYING PRINCIPLE — ALL FOUR ATTACK CERTAINTY:
+  • Broken Vow-Bond: I was certain of US.
+  • Wrong Wish:      I was certain of WHAT I WANTED.
+  • Syzygy:          I was certain of WHAT HAPPENED.
+  • The Fold:        I was certain of WHO I AM.
+
+Not institutions. Not villains. Not paperwork. CERTAINTY. This is the unifying register for every Fatelands HOT crisis. Every opening should arrive as THE MOMENT WHEN A CERTAINTY BREAKS.
+
+ROTATION RULE BY WOUND TYPE — pick the lighthouse the PC's wound architecture demands:
+  • PC wounds about betrayal / abandonment / exposure → BROKEN VOW-BOND (relationship × external; certainty of US)
+  • PC wounds about guilt / complicity / wanting-what-she-shouldn't-have → WRONG WISH (relationship × past choice; certainty of WHAT I WANTED)
+  • PC wounds about loss / regret / could-have-been → SYZYGY (cosmology × past choice; certainty of WHAT HAPPENED)
+  • PC wounds about identity / becoming / self-betrayal → THE FOLD (identity × cosmology; certainty of WHO I AM)
+
+NEVER MORE THAN ONE LIGHTHOUSE PER STORY. Pick the lighthouse the wound architecture points at. The chosen lighthouse defines the emotional register; the pressure menu provides the world-native material; the LI entanglement test welds them.
+
+DO NOT ADD A FIFTH LIGHTHOUSE. The four corners cover the emotional territory: relationship vs identity, past choice vs cosmology. A fifth would either be redundant (collapsing into one of the four) or off-map (no longer Fatelands). If a wound architecture seems to demand a different shape, re-read the wound — it almost certainly fits one of the four.
+
+THE SHARED THEME — across all four:
+  REALITY LISTENS MORE CAREFULLY THAN PEOPLE DO.
+
+A 2024 lawyer cannot explain ANY of these without first being taught how Fate, Wishes, Bonds, Sacrifice, Alignment, and reality itself work in Fatelands. That is the cleanest sign these are genuinely world-native conflicts, not fantasy-flavored paperwork.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+SECONDARY PRESSURE SOURCES (acceptable only when tied to a primary)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+  • succession pressure
+  • political pressure
+  • ceremonial pressure (e.g. First Sacrifice approaching)
+  • family pressure
+  • social pressure
+
+ACCEPTABLE only when tied to Fate, Wish, Sacrifice, Bond, or Oath. A "political pressure" that is just human politics has failed Fatelands.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+FORBIDDEN DEFAULT ENGINES (the reach-for-the-familiar failure)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+Do NOT use these as primary conflict engines:
+  ✗ tribunal / hearing / board / vote / court / audit / review / filing
+  ✗ inheritance paperwork (human legal form)
+  ✗ bureaucratic summons (human form)
+  ✗ paperwork arriving at the door
+  ✗ any conflict that could be described to a 2024 lawyer without explanation
+
+ALLOWED ONLY IF:
+  (a) transformed by Fatelands institutional mechanics (writs as bindings, tribunals probing alignment, boards as oath-witnesses)
+  AND
+  (b) the true underlying engine is one of the PRIMARY PRESSURE categories above
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+SCENE 1 ROMANCE PRIORITY
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+Scene 1 should preferentially organize around:
+  • longing
+  • fascination
+  • temptation
+  • remembered connection
+  • visible bond
+  • fear of losing the bond
+  • desire conflicting with duty
+  • sacrifice connected to the LI
+  • oath connected to the LI
+
+The opening pressure should arrive THROUGH the relationship, not around it.
+
+  ✗ "A writ arrives."
+  ✓ "His name appears in her obligation ledger."
+  ✗ "A tribunal is scheduled."
+  ✓ "Tomorrow she must witness his marriage vow and determine whether it is aligned."
+
+The relationship is the pressure. The institution merely reveals it.
+
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+LITMUS TEST (final check before returning the A-plot)
+═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+If the conflict could be described to a 2024 lawyer WITHOUT explaining Fate, Wishes, Sacrifice, Oaths, Bonds, or Alignment, it is NOT YET a Fatelands conflict. Fatelands stories should feel impossible to relocate into modern reality without breaking the conflict itself.
+
+POSTER TEST: if the Scene 1 poster reads "Woman holding magical paperwork," you have failed. The poster should read like one of:
+  • "His name in her obligation ledger"
+  • "Her bond suddenly visible to strangers"
+  • "The First Sacrifice she has been avoiding"
+  • "The vow she will witness tomorrow and cannot honestly speak herself"
+  • "The wish she made for someone else, rerouting through her"
+
+Fate-anchored, body-anchored, bond-anchored, vow-anchored — not paperwork.
